        <gmd:title><gco:CharacterString>Wildfire susceptibility modelling dataset for British Columbia (2000-2024): conditioning factors at fire and non-fire points</gco:CharacterString></gmd:title>
        <gmd:date><gmd:CI_Date><gmd:date><gco:Date>2026-06-09</gco:Date></gmd:date>
          <gmd:dateType><gmd:CI_DateTypeCode codeListValue="publication" codeList="http://www.isotc211.org/2005/resources/Codelist/gmxCodelists.xml#CI_DateTypeCode">publication</gmd:CI_DateTypeCode></gmd:dateType></gmd:CI_Date></gmd:date>
        <gmd:identifier><gmd:MD_Identifier><gmd:code><gco:CharacterString>doi:10.5281/zenodo.20389083</gco:CharacterString></gmd:code></gmd:MD_Identifier></gmd:identifier>
      </gmd:CI_Citation></gmd:citation>
      <gmd:abstract><gco:CharacterString>Point-level modelling dataset of 1,992 wildfire (burned area >= 70 ha, 2000-2024) and 1,992 spatially independent non-wildfire locations across British Columbia, Canada, each attributed with 18 climatic, vegetation, topographic and anthropogenic conditioning factors used to train LSTM/BiLSTM models optimised with particle swarm optimisation. Companion files provide the 100 ha and 200 ha thresholds and ten random-seed realisations for sensitivity analysis.</gco:CharacterString></gmd:abstract>
