  <gmd:dataQualityInfo><gmd:DQ_DataQuality>
    <gmd:scope><gmd:DQ_Scope><gmd:level><gmd:MD_ScopeCode codeListValue="dataset" codeList="http://www.isotc211.org/2005/resources/Codelist/gmxCodelists.xml#MD_ScopeCode">dataset</gmd:MD_ScopeCode></gmd:level></gmd:DQ_Scope></gmd:scope>
    <gmd:lineage><gmd:LI_Lineage><gmd:statement><gco:CharacterString>Wildfire perimeters (>= 70 ha, 2000-2024) were obtained from the Canadian Wildland Fire Information System and the National Fire Database; spatially independent non-wildfire points were generated with a 20 km exclusion buffer. Conditioning factors were derived from SRTM (topography), ESRI/Sentinel-2 (land cover), TerraClimate and ERA5-Land (climate) and national road, settlement and hydrography layers, resampled to a 1.5 km grid. All layers were projected to NAD83 / BC Albers (EPSG:3005). Predictors were min-max normalised; features were selected by recursive feature elimination on training folds only; models were evaluated with ten-fold spatial-block cross-validation.</gco:CharacterString></gmd:statement></gmd:LI_Lineage></gmd:lineage>
  </gmd:DQ_DataQuality></gmd:dataQualityInfo>
